   "fig_label": "Figure 3",
   "caption": "StRab4 regulates conidial germination and hyphal penetration. (A) Micrographs depicting germ tube, appressorium, and penetration peg formation from individual conidia of the WT and StRab4i strains growing on a cellophane layer over PDA. Images were taken at 6, 12, and 24 h post-inoculation (hpi) (scale bar, 10 μm). (B) Quantification of germ tubes, appressoria, and penetration pegs from conidia of WT and StRab4i strains growing on a cellophane layer over PDA. Asterisks indicate statistical significance, as determined by two-tailed student’s t -test with three independent replicates (* p < 0.05 and ** p < 0.01). Error bars represent the standard deviation (SD) of three replicates. (C) Images depicting penetration by WT and StRab4i strains growing on a cellophane layer over PDA. Images were taken at 5 and 10 days post-inoculation.",
